[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large}, scale=0.75]
\draw[->] (0,0)--(0,9.4);
\draw[->] (0,0)--(11.5,0);
\foreach \y in {20,40,60,80} {\draw (-0.2,\y/10)--(0,\y/10); \node[left,font=\scriptsize] at (-0.2,\y/10) {$\y$};}
\node[left,font=\scriptsize] at (-0.2,0) {$0$};
\draw[thick] (0.8,0)--(2.8,0.8)--(4.8,2.4)--(6.8,5.6)--(8.8,7.2)--(10.8,8.0);
\foreach \p in {(0.8,0),(2.8,0.8),(4.8,2.4),(6.8,5.6),(8.8,7.2),(10.8,8.0)} {\fill \p circle (2.2pt);}
\foreach \x/\lbl in {0.8/0, 2.8/20, 4.8/40, 6.8/60, 8.8/80, 10.8/100} {\draw (\x,0)--(\x,-0.15); \node[below,font=\scriptsize] at (\x,-0.15) {$\lbl$};}
\node[rotate=90] at (-1.4,4.5) {Cumulative frequency};
\node[below] at (5.8,-1.0) {Score};
\node at (5.8,9.0) {Student test scores};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]
The ogive shows the cumulative frequencies of the test scores of $80$ students. Using the segment between $(40, 24)$ and $(60, 56)$, what is the estimated median score?

[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large}, scale=0.75]
\draw[->] (0,0)--(0,11.4);
\draw[->] (0,0)--(11.5,0);
\foreach \y in {50,100,150,200} {\draw (-0.2,\y/20)--(0,\y/20); \node[left,font=\scriptsize] at (-0.2,\y/20) {$\y$};}
\node[left,font=\scriptsize] at (-0.2,0) {$0$};
\draw[thick] (0.8,0)--(2.8,1.5)--(4.8,5.0)--(6.8,8.5)--(8.8,10.0);
\foreach \p in {(0.8,0),(2.8,1.5),(4.8,5.0),(6.8,8.5),(8.8,10.0)} {\fill \p circle (2.2pt);}
\foreach \x/\lbl in {0.8/200, 2.8/400, 4.8/600, 6.8/800, 8.8/1000} {\draw (\x,0)--(\x,-0.15); \node[below,font=\scriptsize] at (\x,-0.15) {$\lbl$};}
\node[rotate=90] at (-1.4,5) {Cumulative frequency};
\node[below] at (4.8,-1.0) {Weekly wage (\$)};
\node at (4.8,11.0) {Employee weekly wages};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]
An ogive plots the weekly wages (in dollars) of $200$ workers. The cumulative frequency curve passes through $(400, 30)$, $(600, 100)$, $(800, 170)$, and $(1000, 200)$. What is the estimated median wage?
